# `s = "$("$n")"` - a string inside an interpolation inside a string.
#
# The case with no stateless reading: the `"` at byte 13 opens a new literal
# rather than closing the one opened at 10, and only a hand carrying the
# interpolation depth can tell those apart. A hand with no memory closes the
# outer literal at 13 and reads `$n")` as code.
#
# Outer [10, 19), inner [13, 17), outer interpolation [11, 18).
roots 1
mends 0
holds string_literal
holds string_interpolation
spans string_literal 10 19
spans string_literal 13 17
spans string_interpolation 11 18
